{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgaa543jc2PoDoG9k75J2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is commit `cd6cf1f` (PR #1943, ticket O3-6093, \"Improve support for arrow functions in expression variable extractor\"). It is in `openmrs-esm-core`, author Ian.\n\nThe change replaces the old `isLocalExpression` flag with a `boundNames` set. Arrow-function parameters are added to that set and passed down into the body, so `x` is excluded there but `b` in `a.map(x => f(b))` is reported. The old code dropped the body's variables when they came back through the return value, which is why only `a` was reported. The new behaviour is covered by the test \"extracts unbound variables from any kind of arrow function body\" (`a.map(x => f(b))` now yields `['a', 'f', 'b']`).\n\nImplementation in esm-core, all in `packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/`:\n- `extractVariableNames()` creates the context and walks the expression. It is the public entry point, exported from `public.ts`.\n- `visitArrowFunctionExpression()` collects the parameter names and visits the body with them bound. This is the core of the fix.\n- `visitIdentifier()` only records a name if it is not a global and not in `boundNames`.\n- `EvaluationContext` and `createContextInternal()` hold the new `boundNames` field in place of `isLocalExpression`.\n- `visitMemberExpression()` no longer uses the local-expression flag. Only computed properties are visited.\n\nSource locations:\n- @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.ts:47-56}\n- @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.ts:111-120}\n- @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.ts:122-129}\n- @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.ts:150-154}\n- @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.ts:158-178}\n- @file:{openmrs-esm-core::packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.test.ts:50-68}\n\nThe commit and PR link come from the commit message and are unverified by Falkon, though the diff confirms the change to `extractor.ts`.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-core\", \"commit\": \"cd6cf1fcbdab85d05529d015dfb911dfef885b84\"},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-core\", \"pr\": 1943},\n  {\"ticket\": \"O3-6093\"},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.ts\", \"startLine\": 111, \"endLine\": 120},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.ts\", \"startLine\": 150, \"endLine\": 154},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.ts\", \"startLine\": 158, \"endLine\": 178},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.ts\", \"startLine\": 47, \"endLine\": 56},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.ts\", \"startLine\": 122, \"endLine\": 129},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-expression-evaluator/src/extractor.test.ts\", \"startLine\": 50, \"endLine\": 68}\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3398,"cache_read_input_tokens":27100,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3398},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9af2707d-98b4-4347-975e-f8cc75c7504d","uuid":"f697358a-7277-44f1-98dc-39aaeec9ccd5","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:43:16.755Z","request_id":"req_011Cgaa53oMWqNVRuAKa3UDn"}
